## 7) Aggregation + ordering + pipelining

### 7.1 Aggregation (no explicit GROUP BY)

Cypher tutorial example:

```cypher
MATCH (u:User)-[:POSTED]->(p:Post)
RETURN u.userID, COUNT(p) AS num_posts
LIMIT 3;
```

Grouping is implied by `u.userID` since `COUNT(p)` is an aggregate. ([Kuzu][2])

### 7.2 ORDER BY

```cypher
MATCH (u:User)-[:POSTED]->(p:Post)
RETURN u.username, COUNT(p) AS num_posts
ORDER BY num_posts DESC
LIMIT 3;
```

([Kuzu][2])

### 7.3 WITH (pipeline / staged query)

Use `WITH` to pass forward computed values, apply top-k, then continue matching:

```cypher
MATCH (u:User)-[:POSTED]->(p:Post)
WITH u, COUNT(p) AS num_posts
ORDER BY num_posts DESC
LIMIT 3
WITH u
MATCH (u2:User)-[:Follows]->(u)
RETURN u.username AS most_prolific_user, u2.username AS follower
LIMIT 8;
```

([Kuzu][2])

