## 9) Subqueries in Kuzu: `EXISTS { ... }` and `COUNT { ... }`

### 9.1 Key rule: Cypher subqueries are `{ ... }` and **cannot contain RETURN**

Kuzu’s Cypher subqueries execute in their own scope, are written in `{}`, and **cannot include a `RETURN` clause**. ([Kuzu][7])

### 9.2 EXISTS subquery

```cypher
MATCH (a:User)
WHERE a.age < 100
  AND EXISTS { MATCH (a)-[:Follows*3..3]->(b:User) }
RETURN a.name, a.age;
```

([Kuzu][7])

Nested EXISTS is also supported. ([Kuzu][7])

### 9.3 COUNT subquery (correlated counting)

Count matches and bind to an alias:

```cypher
MATCH (a:User)
RETURN a.name,
       COUNT { MATCH (a)<-[:Follows]-(b:User) } AS num_follower
ORDER BY num_follower;
```

You can also use `COUNT { ... }` inside `WHERE`, and `COUNT(DISTINCT ...)` patterns are shown in the docs. ([Kuzu][7])

### 9.4 Neo4j difference

`CALL <subquery>` is not supported in Kuzu. ([Kuzu][4])

