## 10) Data modification (CREATE / MERGE / SET / DELETE)

### 10.1 Kuzu’s official guidance

* Kuzu supports `CREATE`, `SET`, `DELETE` (and `MERGE`) for manipulating data
* Use these for **small modifications**
* Use `COPY FROM` for **bulk insertions** ([Kuzu][6])

### 10.2 Labeling best practice in CREATE / MERGE

Kuzu recommends specifying node & relationship labels explicitly in `CREATE` and `MERGE`; otherwise it tries to infer labels from schema. ([Kuzu][4])

### 10.3 SET specifics / limitations vs Neo4j

* Update form: `n.prop = expression`
* Neo4j-style “update a whole property map via `+=`” is **not supported**; update properties one-by-one. ([Kuzu][4])

### 10.4 No REMOVE clause

Neo4j `REMOVE` isn’t supported; use `SET n.prop = NULL` instead. ([Kuzu][4])

