## 11) CALL, “SHOW …”, algorithms, and extensions

### 11.1 Query clauses include CALL

Kuzu lists `CALL` among the “reading” query clauses. ([Kuzu][3])

### 11.2 SHOW becomes CALL show_*()

Neo4j “SHOW …” statements become function calls in Kuzu, e.g.:

* `SHOW FUNCTIONS` (Neo4j) ↔ `CALL show_functions() RETURN *` (Kuzu) ([Kuzu][4])

### 11.3 Graph algorithms are procedures you CALL

Example (K-core):

```cypher
CALL k_core_decomposition('Graph')
RETURN node.name, k_degree
ORDER BY k_degree DESC;
```

([Kuzu][8])

### 11.4 Extensions + version note

Kuzu has an extension mechanism; docs note that in **v0.11.3** four commonly used extensions (`algo`, `fts`, `json`, `vector`) are pre-installed and pre-loaded, and they show `CALL SHOW_OFFICIAL_EXTENSIONS()` style discovery. ([Kuzu][9])

